 "guidelines": "Offsets are JavaScript string indices (UTF-16 code units, e exclusive) into tests/protocol.txt as read by fs.readFileSync(path, \"utf8\") after stripping a UTF-8 BOM if present (the file has none) and replacing CRLF with LF (the committed file is LF; a Windows working copy may be CRLF, so normalise before slicing). \"sha256\" is the hash of that normalised text; refuse the key if it differs. Types: PER, ORG, PLACE (countries, cities, towns, neighbourhoods, streets, sites, facilities). Every mention is keyed, including speaker labels, first names alone and repeats. Titles and role words are outside the span (היו\"ר, מ\"מ היו\"ר, גברת, חבר/חברת הכנסת, השר, מנכ\"ל). \"הכנסת\" inside the title \"חבר הכנסת\" is part of the title and is not keyed. A clitic prefix glued to the first word (ב ל מ ה ו כ ש and combinations, including the definite article ה) is outside the span and recorded in \"prefix\". A ה that belongs to the name itself (הרצלייה) stays in. Public bodies (ministries and their units, Knesset committees, government-appointed committees, municipalities and their departments, regional councils, the army) are ORG with \"public\": true. Universities, NGOs, unions and the health fund are ORG with \"public\": false. Spans are flat: a body named after a place or person (עיריית בת ים, לשכת נווה יעקב, ועדת סילמן) is one ORG mention with no nested PLACE/PER. Descriptive or generic references are not keyed: bare \"הוועדה\", \"המשרד\", \"הארגון\", \"הצבא\", \"הבנק\", \"לאיגוד\", \"שירותי הרווחה\" and \"המחלקה לעבודה סוציאלית\" in running text, \"יום העובדים הסוציאליים\", \"החברה האזרחית\"; nationality adjectives (\"ישראלי\", \"קוריאנית\") are not PLACE. Named units given as someone's affiliation in the invitee list are keyed ORG and marked borderline in \"note\". Blind: written before seeing any model output. Offsets located by script and verified with text.slice(s,e) === surface.",
